                    label   "Trace sets"
                    type    string
                    default { "" }
                    help    "Comma-separated list of names of trace sets that the object is a member of.\n\nBy making an object a member of a trace set, and excluding that trace set with a visibility rule on some other object, the first object can be made invisible to the second object.\n\nFor example, \"grass\" means that the object is a member of a trace set called \"grass\", and \"grass,ball\" means that the object is a member of a trace set called \"grass\" and also a member of another trace set called \"ball\".\n\nIf the text starts with a hyphen, the object will be a member of all trace sets except the ones listed. Setting this to simply \"-\" means that the object is a member of all trace sets.\n\nA trace set name can be any text that does not contain a comma. Spaces are ignored at the start and end of trace set names, and empty trace set names are ignored. Trace set names are case-sensitive.\n"
                    parmtag { "script_action" "import octane_objectparmutils\n\nparm = kwargs[\"parmtuple\"][0]\noctane_objectparmutils.traceSetSelector(parm)" }
